      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 8.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Actually, um, hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.68,
      "end_seconds": 15.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.57,
      "end_seconds": 20.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "I've been feeling tired after the birth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.82,
      "end_seconds": 24.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.47,
      "end_seconds": 33.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, it's been going on for three weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.36,
      "end_seconds": 35.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.15,
      "end_seconds": 44.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "Oh, and bleeding that is tailing off. That's been about the same, about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.09,
      "end_seconds": 51.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Have you been feeling tired after the birth at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.06,
      "end_seconds": 59.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "A bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.76,
      "end_seconds": 82.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "And what about thoughts of harming the baby, leg swelling or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.19,
      "end_seconds": 89.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "no thoughts of harming the baby, leg swelling or fever, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.86,
      "end_seconds": 92.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Ah. Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.64,
      "end_seconds": 95.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.0,
      "end_seconds": 104.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.22,
      "end_seconds": 108.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "yes, trimethoprim i get itching"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.59,
      "end_seconds": 126.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.7,
      "end_seconds": 133.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "I had my appendix taken out when I was in my twenties"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.98,
      "end_seconds": 136.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.11,
      "end_seconds": 147.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.73,
      "end_seconds": 153.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.73,
      "end_seconds": 171.86,
      "duration_seconds": 17.13,
      "text": "It's sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed. I've been reading about it online and it worried me. Paracetamol, 1 gram, when needed. I was on propranolol before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.53,
      "end_seconds": 177.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.02,
      "end_seconds": 180.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "yes, migraines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.7,
      "end_seconds": 189.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "Ah. Yes, migraines is known to us, good to have that clear. Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.67,
      "end_seconds": 205.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.98,
      "end_seconds": 233.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 99 percent, heart rate 65. And respiratory rate 18, pressure 128 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.79,
      "end_seconds": 238.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.81,
      "end_seconds": 242.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.04,
      "end_seconds": 259.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "The womb has gone down well and the stitches are healing, with no redness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.33,
      "end_seconds": 264.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.0,
      "end_seconds": 302.13,
      "duration_seconds": 21.13,
      "text": "okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is a normal postnatal recovery. Let's get a blood count, for postnatal tiredness. Rest when the baby sleeps and ask for help; contraception can be discussed at six weeks. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.19,
      "end_seconds": 305.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.29,
      "end_seconds": 311.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "I'll want another look in four weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.72,
      "end_seconds": 315.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.86,
      "end_seconds": 318.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "take care now"
    }
  ]
